WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.834
[percussion playing]

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.069
 Rich, Dave, congratulations.

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:05.572
You've made it to the final.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.073
Good job.

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.008
It's a second shot at the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:12.111
champion and that
check for $10,000.

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.213
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.583
to create an iconic
blade from history.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:18.584
Rich, you got any ideas?

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.052
 I don't have a clue.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:21.520
 What do you want it to be?

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:22.388
 Lightsaber.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.857
[laughter]

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.693
 Let's see it.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.928
The hook sword.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.763
 Nice.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:33.166
NARRATOR: Long before the hook
sword was featured in films

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.134
like "Crouching
Tiger, Hidden Dragon,"

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.203
it was wielded by the Shaolin
monks in ancient China.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:41.641
Established around 495
AD, the Shaolin monastery

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:45.344
was a hub of martial arts, where
Buddhist monks were trained

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:48.214
in self-defense using
everything from common tools

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.817
to versatile weapons
like the hook sword.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.818
The sword's curved
blade allowed the user

00:00:52.918 --> 00:00:55.288
to trip or disarm opponents.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:59.359
Its crescent guard could be
used to slash or block flows.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.360
And if used in a
pair, the swords

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.829
could be linked at
their hooks to increase

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.731
the weapon's deadly reach.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:06.799
 Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.834
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.136 line:7%
 Good luck.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.073 line:7%
[rock music playing]

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.642
 All right, let's get to work.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.277
Today's day one.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:21.648
I'm excited to be at my own shop
and have a little more comfort.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.916
In my home shop, I don't
have Will screaming

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.052
at me every 45 minutes.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.722
That could be an advantage,
could be a disadvantage.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.124
Ooh, that's hot.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.392
Making this sword is kind
of tough because it's

00:01:32.458 --> 00:01:34.793
the Swiss army knife of swords.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.994
It's got a lot of edges.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.764
It's got a lot of
blocking points.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.169
Today, what I'm
going to do is I'm

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.971
going to make the crescent
part of the blade,

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:47.072
just to work myself into it.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:50.576
It's probably one of the
easier parts of the sword.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:54.613
I'll save the complicated
parts for last.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.682 line:7%
I like it.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.051 line:0%
 The day two plan of
attack's going to be simple.

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:01.688
Get the main portion
of the sword cleaned up

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:05.157
to bare steel and heat treat.

00:02:05.257 --> 00:02:07.393
Looks like it's coming together.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.197
I don't have a quench tank large
enough to do the whole thing.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:13.933
I'll do two heat treats.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.736
I'll do the main post
of the sword first.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.909
It's straight.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.512
And then I'll do
the hook secondly.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:31.083
If I do it this way, the
heat will just hit this part.

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.086
The big concern that
I've got is overheating

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:36.289
the transition
part from the hook

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.490
down into the main
shaft of the sword.

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:43.563
If it's too soft, then on
impact, it can inevitably bend.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:44.931
And I don't want that.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.435
We shall see.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.375 line:0%
 Right now, I'm
happy about the sword.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:58.177
And I'd like to get everything
heat treated by tonight.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.745
In order to get the
heat treat right,

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.580
I'm going to have to
make a bigger forge.

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:05.385
So I'm going to use these drums
that I got from "Breaking Bad"

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:09.322
and turn it into a
heat treat forge.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:09.856
Tah-dah.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.794
This is it.

00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:17.197
Here goes nothing.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.740
I heard weird sounds.

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:38.851
Freaking beautiful.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.653
Not a single twist or bend.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.689 line:0%
I think those noises
may have been coming

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:46.024 line:0%
from the forge barrel
settling, because the heat

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:49.295 line:7%
treat turned out beautiful.

00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:51.463 line:0%
 Today ought to be
a pretty fun day.

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.599 line:0%
Everything's heat treated,
everything's tempered.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.070 line:0%
Just gotta get a handle
put on it and sharpen it.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.373
It should cut, it should
hack, it should stab.

00:04:00.439 --> 00:04:03.142
It should do whatever
they're going to throw at it.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:07.513
I don't want to see
any failure in this.

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:08.014
It cuts.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.284
I'd say that'll work.

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.852
But I'm really not
looking forward

00:04:13.952 --> 00:04:16.355
to what the judges are going
to put this thing up against.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:19.058
Slapping it up against
this or cutting that,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.425
I really don't know.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:23.696
But you know, we're going
to find out soon enough.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.398
I don't like watermelon.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.170 line:0%
 Today, I'm just
debating what type

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.073 line:7%
a handle to put on this thing.

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.909
[bleep]

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.878
I ended up going with a wrap.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.380
I never did macrame.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:42.949
I got the handle wrappped.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:44.284
I got a little
blood on my sword.

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:51.691
As far as the sword design
goes, it's kind of silly.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:53.458
It's got a lot of
sharp edges on it.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.961
It seems a little
dangerous to me.

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:58.031
It's sharp everywhere.

00:05:00.999 --> 00:05:03.302
Well, it will cut.

00:05:03.402 --> 00:05:04.504
We'll see if it will kill.

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:10.009
 Blaesmiths, to test the edge
and sharpness of your blade,

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.145
I will slash one time on
each of these tatami mats

00:05:13.245 --> 00:05:14.479
filled with rice.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.849
If they're sharp, it
should cut cleanly through.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.117
Rich, you're up first.

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:18.817
Are you ready?

00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:20.553
 Heck yeah.

00:05:20.619 --> 00:05:22.054
I think I'm going to do well.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.189
The sword's sharp.

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:24.457
There are no flaws.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.659
There's no inherent
problems with it.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.830
[fast percussion playing]

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:32.532
Nice.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:44.177
Pretty cool.

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:49.115
 Well, Rich-- it is a
light and sharp sword.

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:51.684
You can definitely maneuver
with it for close quarter,

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.385
but as you can
see, you can slash

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:56.188
cleanly through these mats.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:59.325
It definitely will cut.

00:05:59.392 --> 00:06:00.326
 It will.

00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:01.827
 Good job.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:02.428
Dave, you're up next.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:03.195
Are you ready?

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:04.063
 Yes, sir.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:04.764
 Let's do this.

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:11.137
[fast percussion playing]

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.617
Dave, your blade's a
little bit heavier.

00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:28.453
It's sharp enough to
cut, but not sharp enough

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:29.988
to cut all the way through.

00:06:30.088 --> 00:06:33.192
Because of the weight of the
weapon, when you're extending

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:35.928
and you have a point
pointing back at you,

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:37.630
there's a little bit of
concern of how you're

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:40.065
gonna be controlling the blade.

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:42.768
But overall, sir, good job.

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.537
 Thank you.

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:45.804
Rich has a point.

00:06:45.871 --> 00:06:47.974
I don't have a point
yet, so it's 1 to 0.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.210
So I have to fare well
in the second test.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.644
 Dave?

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:54.647
 So gentlemen, to test the
strength of your weapon,

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:57.717
I'm to take two blows against
our terracotta warriors here.

00:06:57.784 --> 00:07:00.052
If your blade is strong
enough, it should survive

00:07:00.152 --> 00:07:02.021
the impact with minimal damage.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:02.821
Rich, are you ready?

00:07:02.921 --> 00:07:03.622
 I am.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:04.157
 OK.

00:07:07.727 --> 00:07:10.830
[hard rock music playing]

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:19.138
Well, Rich, wonderfully
light weapon.

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:20.740
Very, very fast.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.042
You've got a little
deformation on the edge,

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.577
but it didn't chip.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:28.280
Picked up a bit of a bend,
but not too far out of true.

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.748
 Yeah?

00:07:29.848 --> 00:07:32.117
 Well done.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.286
All right, Dave, your turn.

00:07:34.352 --> 00:07:35.454
 I ain't going to watch this.

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:36.555
It's not going to happen.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:39.558
So I'm just using my ears.

00:07:39.625 --> 00:07:42.595
[hard rock music playing]

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.136
I'm good with that.

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:53.873 line:0%
 When I see Dave's sword
shatter the terracotta dummies,

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.941 line:7%
I'm feeling nervous.

00:07:56.008 --> 00:07:58.210
 Well, Dave, a
much heavier weapon.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:01.013
You can see it just powered
right through the terracotta

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.882
with no problem whatsoever.

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:06.151
It's still right and tight,
and true, and everything.

00:08:06.251 --> 00:08:11.857
Little deformation, but again,
we're hitting terracotta.

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.325
Well done.

00:08:13.425 --> 00:08:15.727
 Awesome.

00:08:15.827 --> 00:08:19.465
 Rich, David, the judges
have scrutinized every aspect

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.634
of your work and your
weapons' performances,

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.035
and they've made
their final decision.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.574
David, congratulations.

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:30.209
You are the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:31.110
Good job.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.545
 You're kidding, right?

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:34.747
 No, I'm not.

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:38.683
 Rich, unfortunately, your
weapon did not make the cut.

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.653
 Rich, I love what
you brought us.

00:08:40.719 --> 00:08:42.655
And during the
testing, you and David

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.723
ended up pretty much even.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.292 line:0%
Both of your blades flexed
during the terracotta strength

00:08:47.359 --> 00:08:48.794 line:7%
test.

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:51.463 line:0%
But yours kept the bend in
it, didn't come back to true.

00:08:51.563 --> 00:08:53.132
So that's why we're
sending you home today.

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:54.467
 OK.

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:57.269
 Rich, it's time for you
to surrender your weapon

00:08:57.336 --> 00:08:59.104
and leave the forge.

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:00.505
 Thanks, guys.

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.441
I'm completely happy with
the sword that I made,

00:09:02.508 --> 00:09:05.077
but right now I feel
a little defeated.

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:06.879
I feel a little beat up.

00:09:06.946 --> 00:09:10.149
The first thing I'm doing when I
get home is I'm going to sleep.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:12.418
I could really use a nap.

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:16.722
 Dave, you came in just shy
the first time you were here.

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:19.325
Now you're a "Forged in
Fire" champion who's also

00:09:19.391 --> 00:09:22.695
receiving a check for $10,000.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:23.896
How do you feel right now?

00:09:23.963 --> 00:09:25.331
 I honestly don't
know right now.

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:27.199
I'm still kind of
elated at the moment.

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:28.500
[laughter]

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.069
 I like the way the
edge held up on that.

00:09:30.135 --> 00:09:32.938
Didn't take any chips
or chunks out of it.

00:09:33.038 --> 00:09:33.639
 Thank you.

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:34.840
 Well, congratulations.

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:41.647
 Now I've actually proven to
myself that, yes, I can do it.

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:44.984
And getting to go home
as a champion, that's--

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:46.185
that's pretty cool.

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:49.188
[hard rock music playing]

